From: Vetrivelan Velmurugan <vetri96muruga@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:32:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] backend: system_event on Socket.IO; battery lockout confirmed
 and PAUSEs

1. system_event (new socket event, system_event@1)
   mission_manager sends OBSTACLE_PAUSED/CLEARED, RTK_FLOAT/PAUSED/RECOVERED,
   ODOM_PAUSED, ESTOP_ACTIVE/RELEASED and MISSION_COMPLETED on
   /mission_manager/point_event without a point_id. ros_bridge only spoke
   them (voice); the tablet never received them. They are now queued on the
   same ordered queue as point events and emitted as `system_event`
   (original fields + event_kind=SYSTEM + schema). Point events unchanged.

2. Battery critical lockout (follow-up to 9268a87/1e587d9/1097940)
   - Confirmed, not single-sample: >= 3 consecutive samples <= 23.80 V over
     >= 8 s (/mavros/battery measured ~0.3 Hz). Unlock needs 2 consecutive
     samples >= 24.20 V (hysteresis). Pure BatteryLockoutFilter.
   - The automatic action is PAUSE (progress preserved), not STOP, and only
     while RUNNING, per docs/DYX_Mission_Power_Cycle_Recovery_Logic.md
     "Battery Critical Case". START/RESUME/NEXT/SKIP stay refused by the
     existing route check (which still also refuses on an instantaneous
     <= 10 % sample; conservative for starting motion).
   - Telemetry field names (battery_critical_stop_*) unchanged for the
     tablet (ae5f711 reads them).

Not included: manual-drive API (needs a design), battery stream rate (which
MAVLink message feeds /mavros/battery at 0.3 Hz is not yet established).

Tests: 676 passed locally; the one failure
(test_signature_changes_on_lifecycle_change[change11]) predates this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
